config SYNCHROFLY_SCHEDULING_MTM_MAX_SLOTS
	int "max slots for a MTM schedule"
	default 100
	help
	  This option primarily exists as an example of a library Kconfig
	  setting.

	  This option specifies the value for custom_get_value() to return
	  when the input parameter is zero. (Otherwise the function returns the
	  input parameter value.)

config CONTENTION_PARTICIPATION_PROBABILITY
	int "Contention participation probability (%)"
	default 80
	range 0 100
	help
	  Probability (in percentage) that a node will participate in ranging
	  during contention-based MTM blocks. This controls network load and
	  interference levels. 100% means all nodes always participate,
	  while lower values create random participation patterns.

config SYNCHROFLY_SCHEDULING_SLOT_PADDING_US
	int "Slot duration padding time in microseconds"
	default 50
	range 10 1000
	help
	  Padding time added to calculated slot duration to compensate for
	  unaccounted timing factors in the ideal slot calculation. The need
	  for significant padding (e.g., 200us) indicates missing components
	  in the slot duration model such as radio state transitions, interrupt
	  latencies, or processing delays. Higher values ensure reliable
	  operation but reduce throughput.